question:
What is the maximum electron population in each of the following?
(i) $n = 2$ shell;
(ii) $3d$ subshell;
(iii) $4p_y$ sub-orbital.

The osmotic pressure of a solution prepared by dissolving $1.0\text{ g}$ of haemoglobin in $100\text{ cm}^3$ of water is $0.413\text{ kPa}$ at $20^\circ\text{C}$. Calculate
(a) concentration in the unit of $\text{g m}^{-3}$;
(b) the molar mass of the haemoglobin.

In each of the following pair, identify molecular species with the higher entropy [assuming constant temperature except in (c)]
(a) $1\text{ mole}$ of solid $\text{KBr}$ or $1\text{ mole}$ of an aqueous $\text{KBr}$;
(b) $1\text{ mole}$ of $\text{SO}_2$ or $1\text{ mole}$ of $\text{SO}_3$;
(c) sea water in mid-winter at $2^\circ\text{C}$ or in mid-summer at $23^\circ\text{C}$;
(d) $3\text{ moles}$ of oxygen gas or $2\text{ moles}$ of ozone gas;
(e) $1\text{ mole}$ of $\text{CO}_2$ solid or $1\text{ mole}$ of $\text{CO}_2$ gas.

State the number of phases in each of the following:
(a) air;
(b) a mixture containing oil and water;
(c) a mixture of salt and sand;
(d) a mixture of ethanol and water;
(e) addition of $\text{CaCO}_3$ to a mixture containing $\text{CaO}$ and $\text{CO}_2$ gas.

State and account for the trend in the properties listed in (b) above:
(i) across a period;
(ii) down a group in the periodic table. (12 marks)
